; HOW THIS WORKS
; Every layer is a full-resolution 7680x1080 picture drawn at 0.75 (= 5760 x 810 px in the world),
; almost 1 picture pixel per screen pixel, so it is sharp.
; Each layer is drawn twice (second copy mirrored) and repeats every 11520 px, so it never ends.
; Parallax2D scroll_scale.x = how fast the layer slides sideways with the camera.
; metadata/vertical_parallax = how much it follows the camera up and down.
; metadata/cover_top = world y of the top of the picture: forest_background.gd makes sure this
; top always stays above the screen (any window size, fullscreen, zoom or jump height).
; Trees, mist and ground share the same values, so tree roots always stay planted in the ground.

